.TH SDL_StartTextInputWithProperties 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_StartTextInputWithProperties \- Start accepting Unicode text input events in a window, with properties describing the input.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_keyboard.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_StartTextInputWithProperties(SDL_Window *window, SDL_PropertiesID props);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function will enable text input
.BR "" ( SDL_EVENT_TEXT_INPUT
and
.BR SDL_EVENT_TEXT_EDITING
events) in the specified window\[char46] Please use this function paired with
.BR SDL_StopTextInput ()\[char46]
.PP
Text input events are not received by default\[char46]
.PP
On some platforms using this function shows the screen keyboard and/or activates an IME, which can prevent some key press events from being passed through\[char46]
.PP
These are the supported properties:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_TYPE_NUMBER
- an
.BR SDL_TextInputType
value that describes text being input, defaults to
.BR SDL_TEXTINPUT_TYPE_TEXT \[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_CAPITALIZATION_NUMBER
- an
.BR SDL_Capitalization
value that describes how text should be capitalized, defaults to
.BR SDL_CAPITALIZE_SENTENCES
for normal text entry,
.BR SDL_CAPITALIZE_WORDS
for
.BR SDL_TEXTINPUT_TYPE_TEXT_NAME ,
and
.BR SDL_CAPITALIZE_NONE
for e-mail addresses, usernames, and passwords\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_AUTOCORRECT_BOOLEAN
- true to enable auto completion and auto correction, defaults to true\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_MULTILINE_BOOLEAN
- true if multiple lines of text are allowed\[char46] This defaults to true if
.BR SDL_HINT_RETURN_KEY_HIDES_IME
is \(dq0\(dq or is not set, and defaults to false if
.BR SDL_HINT_RETURN_KEY_HIDES_IME
is \(dq1\(dq\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_TITLE_STRING
- a title for the top of the on-screen keyboard window, if it has one\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_PLACEHOLDER_STRING
- the placeholder shown before the user starts typing, when the field is empty\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_DEFAULT_TEXT_STRING
- text to prefill the text field with\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_MAX_LENGTH_NUMBER
- maximum length for the text field, in characters (not bytes)\[char46]
.PP
On Android you can directly specify the input type:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_ANDROID_INPUTTYPE_NUMBER
- the text input type to use, overriding other properties\[char46] This is documented at https://developer\[char46]android\[char46]com/reference/android/text/InputType
.PP
On HarmonyOS/OpenHarmony you can directly specify the input type:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTINPUT_OPENHARMONY_INPUTTYPE_NUMBER
- the text input type to use, overriding other properties\[char46] This is documented at https://developer\[char46]android\[char46]com/reference/android/text/InputType

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I window
the window to enable text input\[char46]
.TP
.I props
the properties to use\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_SetTextInputArea (3),
.BR SDL_StartTextInput (3),
